{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/389252-do-demons-get-the-memories-of-the-cover","id":389252,"title":"Do demons get the memories of the cover?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-01T19:17:52-08:00","id":389252,"title":"Do demons get the memories of the cover?","content":"When a pact is signed does a demon get the memories associated with a cover? using the &quot;abusive&quot; partner example, would the demon actually have the memories associated with the abuse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T19:26:07-08:00","id":389302,"title":"","content":"Nope. It's one of the reasons why a demon should do extensive research about the relationship she's buying before adding it to one of her Covers. Some of this stuff is easy to &quot;fake it until you make it,&quot; but some of it really, really isn't, and it seems like a waste to go through all the trouble of getting someone to agree to a Pact only to lose the points of Cover it grants because you completely fail to act in-character for the stuff you bought. Sounds like the kind of thing seasoned Tempters at Agencies laugh up their sleeves about - a real rookie error.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T20:00:50-08:00","id":389335,"title":"","content":"P. 117 &quot;It\u2019s not all perfect, though. Stealing someone\u2019s life doesn\u2019t actually give the demon any of that person\u2019s memories, knowledge, or personality. Smart demons don\u2019t take the step of calling in a soul pact unless they know the target fairly well, lest they degrade the new Cover straightaway by acting grossly out of character.&quot; <br /> <br /> In theory, activating Legend could get you access to those bits of memory, but that has drawbacks of its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T07:36:45-08:00","id":408946,"title":"","content":"Would it be possible for a demon to make a pact to receive someone's memories? If so, then this could be done before the soulpact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5082-lorsa","name":"Lorsa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T10:03:59-08:00","id":409067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lorsa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/389252-do-demons-get-the-memories-of-the-cover?p=408946#post408946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be possible for a demon to make a pact to receive someone's memories? If so, then this could be done before the soulpact?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no existing mechanic for this, no. Taking someone's identity requires a lot of intelligence gathering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T16:50:16-08:00","id":409410,"title":"","content":"There is, however, a Demon Form ability for reading minds. So, there is that, if you want to spend the Process slot on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T16:55:02-08:00","id":409415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/389252-do-demons-get-the-memories-of-the-cover?p=409410#post409410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is, however, a Demon Form ability for reading minds. So, there is that, if you want to spend the Process slot on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also remember that you're one of the premier liars on the face of the planet, and a few dots in Subterfuge and a good selection of Embeds you'll have a lot more breathing room than you'd expect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T01:03:09-08:00","id":409784,"title":"","content":"If all else fails figure out what you to do to survive slamming your head into the ground after getting hit by a car. You can then use the trauma from the accident to write off some of the inconsistencies and memory gaps as residual trauma. I would advise that as a severe option because that is going to hurt, draw attention and if there's a sudden influx of retrograde amnesia brought on by car accidents excess attention might show up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T14:00:42-08:00","id":410521,"title":"","content":"Or, less drastically: move. Less chances for someone connected to you to call out inconsistencies, you can blame inconsistencies on the pressures of the new environment, unless they come meet you face to face it's pretty easy to shutdown a conversation that's heading in the wrong direction, all sorts of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T15:45:42-08:00","id":410653,"title":"","content":"Moving, I suspect, will be a hell of a Compromise Check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T21:40:42-08:00","id":411024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/389252-do-demons-get-the-memories-of-the-cover?p=410521#post410521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, less drastically: move. Less chances for someone connected to you to call out inconsistencies, you can blame inconsistencies on the pressures of the new environment, unless they come meet you face to face it's pretty easy to shutdown a conversation that's heading in the wrong direction, all sorts of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read it in a while, but I'm pretty sure that &quot;acting grossly out of character&quot; isn't something that an observer has to &quot;call out&quot; to create a Compromise check. Unless I'm wrong, I was under the impression that &quot;reality&quot; the &quot;God-machine&quot; or whatever you wanted to call it, knew how &quot;Sally&quot; was supposed to act and if &quot;she&quot; started acting weird then it would take notice. Otherwise, killing someone in cold blood (albeit an extreme example) wouldn't cause a Compromise roll so long as no one who knew Sally was around to see it.<br /> <br /> As a matter of fact, the text quoted earlier by MCN backs me up &quot;p 117....Smart demons don\u2019t take the step of calling in a soul pact unless they know the target fairly well, lest they degrade the new Cover straightaway by acting grossly out of character.&quot; It's reasonable to assume a demon isn't going to be calling in those pacts with a bunch of friends and family surrounding the target. So it seems pretty reasonable to assume the demon is then completely alone when she begins &quot;degrad[ing] the new Cover straightaway by acting grossly out of character.&quot;<br /> <br /> So moving doesn't seem like it would do a thing, except, as MCN pointed out, likely be quite a Compromise Check for most people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T09:11:40-08:00","id":411662,"title":"","content":"Unless, of course, the person whose identity you're taking is a drifter, or someone who moves periodically due to work, or who was about to move... you can time that shit, too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T14:47:24-08:00","id":413166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiarn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/389252-do-demons-get-the-memories-of-the-cover?p=411024#post411024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't read it in a while, but I'm pretty sure that &quot;acting grossly out of character&quot; isn't something that an observer has to &quot;call out&quot; to create a Compromise check. Unless I'm wrong, I was under the impression that &quot;reality&quot; the &quot;God-machine&quot; or whatever you wanted to call it, knew how &quot;Sally&quot; was supposed to act and if &quot;she&quot; started acting weird then it would take notice. Otherwise, killing someone in cold blood (albeit an extreme example) wouldn't cause a Compromise roll so long as no one who knew Sally was around to see it.<br /> <br /> As a matter of fact, the text quoted earlier by MCN backs me up &quot;p 117....Smart demons don\u2019t take the step of calling in a soul pact unless they know the target fairly well, lest they degrade the new Cover straightaway by acting grossly out of character.&quot; It's reasonable to assume a demon isn't going to be calling in those pacts with a bunch of friends and family surrounding the target. So it seems pretty reasonable to assume the demon is then completely alone when she begins &quot;degrad[ing] the new Cover straightaway by acting grossly out of character.&quot;<br /> <br /> So moving doesn't seem like it would do a thing, except, as MCN pointed out, likely be quite a Compromise Check for most people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first: I think if the demon approaches it right - complaining about needing to find a new job, then talking about how you found one in another city, etc. - it doesn't necessarily have to be acting grossly out of character, though I agree that moving without any notice right out of the blue is a pretty good candidate. However, in this situation I'd probably risk the Compromise check.<br /> <br /> This situation, of course, is a little different then how you portray, because I'm not suggesting moving because if you do so you'll suddenly be free of Compromise due to lack of people noticing you're out of character. This entire thread is about how a demon doesn't get any of the memories associated with his or her new cover. If you're in a situation where you're constantly surrounded by people that can catch those niggling inconsistencies between the pactee and the demon's memories and personalities and use them to completely unravel your cover over time - which I don't think most demons would get themselves into knowingly, but it could definitely happen - I think risking a single Compromise by moving away from that environment of extreme scrutiny is worth the risk.<br /> <br /> And I guess it should be noted that when I said that this was a less drastic option, I was comparing it to staging a car accident so you can fake a head-trauma induced personality change a la Fred Flinstone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T03:19:57-08:00","id":413942,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://s57.photobucket.com/user/Dameric/media/Crazy2.jpg.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i57.photobucket.com/albums/g216/Dameric/Crazy2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5032-jackofshadows","name":"Jackofshadows","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}